<h1 class="article-title">Notice of Lease Rights Auction for Property at Pulvera Street 29</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p><strong>Notice of unsuccessful auction.</strong> The Liepāja Special Economic Zone Authority, unified registration No. LV90000329402, registered address Fēniksa Street 4, Liepāja, LV-3401, announces that its written auction of lease rights for the property under its management at Pulvera Street 29, Liepāja, cadastral No. 1700 010 0303, has been declared unsuccessful. The lease property consists of portions of land totalling 5,397 m² and six buildings: “Administration Building” (1700 010 0303 001), “Boiler House” (1700 010 0303 002), “Oil-Containing Wastewater Treatment Facilities” (1700 010 0303 003), “Pump House” (1700 010 0303 004), “Distribution Station” (1700 010 0303 005), and “Receiving Station” (1700 010 0303 006), together with Authority-owned engineering structures, including installations and tanks, supporting the wastewater treatment complex.</p><p>____________________________</p><p>The Authority informs that, by order of its Chief Executive dated <strong>18 May 2026</strong>, the deadline for approving the auction results under Clause 5.8 of the auction rules was extended to <strong>27 May 2026</strong>, as the next Board meeting scheduled to approve the results would take place on that date.</p><p>____________________________</p><p>The Authority clarifies the notice published on <strong>1 August 2025</strong> concerning the property auction at Pulvera Street 29. The notice should correctly read as follows:</p><p>“Registration of bidders takes place from <strong>1 August 2025 at 08:00</strong> to <strong>12 September 2025 at 16:30</strong>. Bidders must submit their offers in person or through an authorised representative to the Authority at Fēniksa Street 4, Liepāja, by 12 September 2025, during working hours 08:00–12:00 and 12:30–16:30. Offers will be opened on <strong>16 September 2025 at 13:00</strong>.”</p><p>The Liepāja Special Economic Zone Authority (hereinafter the Authority), unified registration No. LV90000329402, registered address Fēniksa Street 4, Liepāja, LV-3401, is organising a written auction of lease rights for the property it manages at Pulvera Street 29, Liepāja (cadastral No. 1700 010 0303). The property consists of land portions totalling 5,397 m² and the following six buildings: Administration Building (1700 010 0303 001); Boiler House (1700 010 0303 002); Oil-Containing Wastewater Treatment Facilities (1700 010 0303 003); Pump House (1700 010 0303 004); Distribution Station (1700 010 0303 005); Receiving Station (1700 010 0303 006); and Authority-owned engineering structures such as installations and tanks used to operate the oil-containing wastewater treatment complex.</p><p>The objective is to determine the tenant who submits the most economically advantageous offer for the lease rights and undertakes, throughout the lease term, to receive waste delivered by vessels calling at the Port of Liepāja under the vessel sanitary dues pursuant to MARPOL Annex I and to ensure its treatment in accordance with legal requirements.</p><p><strong>Initial monthly rent:</strong> EUR 2,087.00 (two thousand and eighty-seven euros and 00 cents), excluding VAT. <strong>Auction security deposit:</strong> EUR 6,000.00 (six thousand euros and 00 cents). Before submitting an application, bidders must transfer the deposit to the Authority, registration No. LV90000329402, AS “Swedbank”, account No. <strong>LV12HABA0001407037000</strong>, with the payment reference “Security deposit for participation in the written auction of lease rights for real estate at Pulvera Street 29, Liepāja”.</p><p>Participants are required to familiarise themselves with the documents relating to the leased property and its treatment facilities and inspect the property in person, agreeing on the visit time beforehand. If the bidder inspected the property during the first lease rights auction, or declines inspection for objective reasons, they must submit a signed statement with their application confirming that they inspected the property in the first auction or know and accept its condition and waive future claims concerning that condition.</p><p>For information about the auction documentation, call <strong>26449898</strong>.</p></div>
</div>
